<title>THAILAND: Thailand pegs 1997/98 coffee at 75,700 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Thailand pegs 1997/98 coffee at 75,700 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Agriculture Ministry on Monday kept its 1997/98 coffee output forecast unchanged at 75,700 tonnes.  </p>
<p>The planting area was projected at 65,920 hectares with the yield seen at 1.15 tonnes per hectare, a ministry official said.</p>
<p>Farmers were watching the price trend before deciding whether to raise production, the official added.</p>
<p>Thailand exports only small amount of robusta coffee each year. The 1996/97 government export target was 53,000 tonnes. The target for 1997/98 crop will be set in October.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
